    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 0,
        "sourceEnd": 237,
        "text": "Museum director Anna: Good morning, everyone. Thank you for coming to this early meeting. We need to decide how to present the new exhibition about the ancient water clock. As you know, the clock is broken, and we have only a few pieces.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
        "textHash": "22ac9ba9686340e61abf210b5d05be4d369a780fa3bef350f1e9e4958a8be800",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "curator ben",
        "speaker": "Curator Ben",
        "sourceStart": 252,
        "sourceEnd": 396,
        "text": "Right. The problem is that we don't know exactly how the clock worked. Some parts are missing. We have a drawing from 1890, but it may be wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4dc9e5e54ebad3be90ef6c66e4a8ade0388c987718918c806552551141ba8f22",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 404,
        "sourceEnd": 550,
        "text": "So we must be careful. We can't say 'this is how it worked' if we are not sure. Maybe we should show the drawing and the real pieces side by side.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "dc7df8b5ba94778e115a9d5d0715b3cac2d0f1f69100b04eb149409395dc5f1f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 557,
        "sourceEnd": 655,
        "text": "I agree. But visitors might think the drawing is a photo of the real clock. We need a clear label.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "cb83706f9a9970549f003244ad62c32d17673a16254102420f39cf27cc5e6531",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 657,
        "sourceEnd": 849,
        "text": "Education officer Chen: I have an idea. We can put a question mark on the label. For example: 'How did the water flow? We are not sure.' That way, visitors know that the evidence is uncertain.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
        "textHash": "5b38726bea320ac150b98fe0326a63f4ed4a42ad3d9fdabbdd187681ad92bf1b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 857,
        "sourceEnd": 1015,
        "text": "That's good. But we also need to think about privacy. Some of the letters we found mention a family name. We should not show the full name without permission.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "1e9e0548d18b4cd1658a471ce48fc1360014de47b4f77cff17e777678d17ae37",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1022,
        "sourceEnd": 1130,
        "text": "True. The letters are from a private collection. The owner said we can show them, but we must hide the name.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "75fd1eaa40df98d4d64074dd3e3f78e5a06dbe935f3f2f69f64c7a51074435b5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "chen",
        "speaker": "Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1138,
        "sourceEnd": 1232,
        "text": "So we can cover the name with a black line. And we can explain that we are protecting privacy.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "33afd45786fd250ffa369d9a2f325db84169fe5d4df6e7d47dc8558d90d9756f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1240,
        "sourceEnd": 1430,
        "text": "Perfect. Now, about the technology. We want to add a small screen that shows a 3D model. But the model is only a guess. We must tell visitors that it is a reconstruction, not the real thing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "5ea19f1299e3ce5b6ecdc7006cbf8cbb3f9a00fd9cf155425587fae92af0fe66",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1437,
        "sourceEnd": 1561,
        "text": "I can write a short text for the screen. Something like: 'This model is based on our best ideas, but it may not be correct.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "481db072914f32b26d3bc335ad1e3dd811d5a4af40a0ea976d48448240f4e06a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "chen",
        "speaker": "Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1569,
        "sourceEnd": 1699,
        "text": "And we can ask visitors what they think. Maybe a small voting station: 'Do you think the water flowed from the top or the bottom?'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "7462034b8dbad6ec0233f964d4e23164ddf2e0e7f426c9977d775bb83d8bfca1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1707,
        "sourceEnd": 1818,
        "text": "I like that. It makes people think about evidence. But we must not say that one answer is right. We don't know.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "48f6e6ae40e081457e70947c91a62eca7edeaf18f04470fe93f655dbed7ee93b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1825,
        "sourceEnd": 1875,
        "text": "So the exhibition is about questions, not answers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ed10f3e63b3d6e362e9195cd4e0d25649c78ec44398290e5632553e00cbbdf55",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1883,
        "sourceEnd": 2004,
        "text": "Exactly. Let's also remember that some visitors may not read English well. We should use simple words and maybe pictures.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "b5463ca42d54e4615c6068bf1ed3331e8a7954de80752a8741f5f42da9d0c940",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "chen",
        "speaker": "Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2012,
        "sourceEnd": 2139,
        "text": "I can make a simple guide with short sentences. And we can train the staff to say: 'We are not sure, but here is what we know.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "997b0bf9c1872a0b52e5c051e59e71cd82c1e3dd4d9100220d44a86ab48dcfc1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 2147,
        "sourceEnd": 2325,
        "text": "Good. So to summarize: we will show the real pieces, the old drawing with a question mark, the letters with the name hidden, and the 3D model with a clear warning. Any questions?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a08e5a586e30f561f460985d5ac83bd48ad8aab496a3a33e9f3bd0060d83e16b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2332,
        "sourceEnd": 2373,
        "text": "Just one. When do we need the final text?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "71d06c3d29c02de5d3079c774fac6c83c9283a689794fc77bbb0153d00147ed3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 2381,
        "sourceEnd": 2420,
        "text": "By Friday, please. Thank you, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "66aa65d7e06e410b1b683e279bb2a3ffe8ac3caa8e243c6bb1b01ede081e8f23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
